From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jake Hoffman <122403457+jakethehoffer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:05:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] snappy: take byte-order helpers from gulliver.h on QNX

snappy's compat.h includes <endian.h> on every system that is not FreeBSD,
macOS or Windows to get htole16() and le32toh(). The QNX SDP 8.0 has no
<endian.h>; the equivalent macros are ENDIAN_LE16() and ENDIAN_LE32() in
<gulliver.h>.

Add a QNX branch that defines the two names from gulliver.h.

Signed-off-by: Jake Hoffman <122403457+jakethehoffer@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 lib/snappy-fef67ac/compat.h | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lib/snappy-fef67ac/compat.h b/lib/snappy-fef67ac/compat.h
index 3b755f4..4e71fa3 100644
--- a/lib/snappy-fef67ac/compat.h
+++ b/lib/snappy-fef67ac/compat.h
@@ -18,6 +18,10 @@
 #endif
 
 
+#elif defined(__QNXNTO__)
+#  include <gulliver.h>
+#  define	htole16(x) ENDIAN_LE16(x)
+#  define	le32toh(x) ENDIAN_LE32(x)
 #elif !defined(__WIN32__)
 #  include <endian.h>
 #endif
